{"l":4381,"g":6,"b":1,"cefr":"A2","role":"reinforcement","insight":"conceptual_bridge","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'While Dad was cooking, the children ___ the table.'","o":["was setting","are setting","sets","were setting"],"a":"were setting","r":"To handlinger i gang samtidig i fortiden: 'the children were setting'."},
{"l":4411,"g":6,"b":1,"cefr":"A2","role":"reinforcement","insight":"conceptual_bridge","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når du vil spørge en ven, om du må låne hans cykel i dag?","o":["Can I borrow your bike today?","Can I lend your bike today?","Can you borrow me your bike today?","Can I borrow you bike today?"],"a":"Can I borrow your bike today?","r":"Den, der får noget, siger 'borrow'. Den, der giver, siger 'lend'."},
{"l":4438,"g":6,"b":1,"cefr":"A2","role":"reinforcement","insight":"conceptual_bridge","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'I need ___ eggs for the cake. Can you buy them?'","o":["any","some","much","a"],"a":"some","r":"I bekræftende sætninger bruger vi 'some'. 'Eggs' kan tælles, så ikke 'much'."},
{"l":4471,"g":6,"b":1,"cefr":"A2","role":"reinforcement","insight":"conceptual_bridge","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'First, mix the flour and the sugar. Then add two eggs and some milk.' Hvad skal man gøre først?","o":["komme æg i","hælde mælk i","blande mel og sukker","tænde ovnen"],"a":"blande mel og sukker","r":"'First' betyder først, og først skal man blande mel og sukker."},
{"l":4495,"g":6,"b":1,"cefr":"A2","role":"reinforcement","insight":"conceptual_bridge","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'My grandmother ___ drinks tea in the afternoon, almost every day.'","o":["never","rarely","hardly","usually"],"a":"usually","r":"'Almost every day' betyder næsten hver dag, så det passer med 'usually'."},
